{
 "about": "Front JA0: the ja glossary (plan analysis/front-plans/front-i18n-ja.md §5) that src/i18n/ja/ja.test.ts enforces through the SC4 lint framework (src/i18n/lint/, profile ja) on every Japanese string. Seeded from the French glossary: the same English patterns and interface names, re-targeted to Japanese from the English (French only as meaning context) following the JA0 style brief. A term applies when its English pattern matches the English source: the Japanese must then match the `ja` pattern (flags iu). Matching is by plain substring, with no word boundaries, because Japanese has no spaces. Names are fixed interface names (an exact name applies only to a whole string; the English name is matched as written) and must appear literally in the Japanese. Forbidden here are the term forms this glossary rejects (レッドシフト, クラスター for a star cluster, 視等級, 消光, 発光線 and 放射線 for a line, スペクトロメーター, フォトメーター, ケフェイド (the IAU OAE writes セファイド), and あなた; the katakana long vowel is the ja profile's own rule); the language-wide rules (typography with full-width marks and 「」, no spaces between Japanese and Latin text, the です/ます register, kanji-only Chinese forms, claims that a translation is CLEA's or official) live in the ja profile of src/i18n/lint/profiles.ts. VIREO's own names follow the brief's decided forms (Save → 保存, Record → 記録, Find → 探す, Search → 検索, Show/Display/View → 表示, Slew → 移動, Init/Go → 初期化/開始, Scan → 順に表示, Clear → クリア, Delete → 削除, Reset → リセット, Hot List → 天体リスト, lab → 実習, Object X → 天体X). Rows for areas still in English wait for their sub-front. Translations are web adaptations by OpenVireo, never CLEA's.",
